{"id": "EUVD-2026-82908", "enisaUuid": "1eea3346-532c-333e-bc59-17ed7bbe6757", "description": "ImageMagick before 7.1.2-31 and 6.9.13-56 contains a division-by-zero flaw in the FLIF encoder. An incorrect value for ticks per second in the image being encoded causes a divide-by-zero and crashes the encoder, resulting in a denial of service. The issue is fixed in 7.1.2-31 and 6.9.13-56.", "datePublished": "2026-09-18T13:20:03", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-18T14:39:36", "baseScore": 6.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-4gg2-hfgh-6f5c", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/imagemagick-before-7.1.2-31-division-by-zero-in-flif-encoder"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93589", "GHSA-gqxf-6h36-mg34"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.33, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "80230754-be1a-3c12-9033-16f520c546cd", "product": {"name": "ImageMagick", "vendor": {"name": "ImageMagick"}}, "product_version": "0 <6.9.13-56"}, {"id": "9df8b8db-7792-3d56-9a01-0dbdf3ce1f35", "product": {"name": "ImageMagick", "vendor": {"name": "ImageMagick"}}, "product_version": "0 <7.1.2-31"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "465817a2-8f28-3cbd-89d8-e638f31526f9", "vendor": {"name": "ImageMagick"}}], "isExploited": false}